# Entry Main: a field of the result may be named as a local of C (step 21.7 K3, part 2). C declares `int: x 5`;
# the description names a field x. The items are read in the scope of C: x 6, y 7; the local x stays 5. observed
# 67.
@: result 0
int: observed 0
D:
    return:
        int: x
        int: y
    end: return
    C:
        int: x 5
        return: x + 1 x + 2
    end: C
end: D
---
Main:
    node\result := D\C()
    node\observed := node\result\x * 10 + node\result\y
